From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shayne Legault <8741557+shaynelegault@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:50:16 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: SMP: restore the standard secondary FIQ state

AIC1 dispatches interrupts through the normal IRQ path. Restore
secondary_start_kernel()'s interrupt state for ARM instead of leaving
FIQ masked for every machine in a multi-platform kernel.

Link: https://github.com/OrchardLinux/orchard/issues/79
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Shayne Legault <8741557+shaynelegault@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm/kernel/smp.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/kernel/smp.c b/arch/arm/kernel/smp.c
index 2d46adad3..3431c0553 100644
--- a/arch/arm/kernel/smp.c
+++ b/arch/arm/kernel/smp.c
@@ -469,8 +469,7 @@ asmlinkage void secondary_start_kernel(struct task_struct *task)
 	complete(&cpu_running);
 
 	local_irq_enable();
-	/* Cascadia: the A5's AIC delivers everything as IRQ; FIQ stays off on
-	 * secondaries until something is known to need it. */
+	local_fiq_enable();
 	local_abt_enable();
 
 	/*
